## Assumptions and limitations
The 2021 assay is a relative fluorescent surface/internal partition in transfected GFP-positive singlets, with separate GFP expression (not PMP22-GFP fusion), antibody brightness calibration and below-background signals assigned zero. It is not calibrated molecules per viable cell or a synthesis rate. The 2014 assay uses C-terminal GFP-tagged human PMP22 in HeLa, actin-normalized glycoform blots and localization; it calls CHX treatment a pulse-chase, but there is no pulse-labelled protein cohort. Culture experiments/cells/KO clones must not be relabelled independent patients. Endo H resistance is post-ER/cis-Golgi transit, not surface or functional myelin. N41Q lacks the glycan substrate and requires a separate detection interpretation. Neither source supplies the matched functional-rescue endpoint for these perturbations.

Contradictions retained rather than repaired: 2021 UGGT1 abstract versus Results/Discussion; CNX KD/GFP/HeLa versus KO/myc/HEK293 differences; LMAN1 binding without appreciable trafficking change; L16P versus G150D RER1 response; 2014 Hrd1 siRNA #1 reduction of gp78 (Supplement S2); 2021 supplement S8 extracted 10 mM versus main Fig 4 10 micromolar dose tokens; 2021 S10B caption WT/UGGT1 wording while main Results cite mutant total-level effects. Total-direction statements from the latter panels remain main-text-reported, not independently digitized values. No undocumented correction or dose recommendation.

Inherited outcomes preserved: GSE241269 locked Pmp22-myelin7 contrast -0.0365 (interval -0.241,+0.168) failed, not equivalence. Osgin1 measured but below baseline floor makes the original five-gene antioxidant test untestable; four-gene result retrospective, no NRF2 mediation. Ppp6r1/Gtf2f1/Hck transfer failed in locked Zeb2 tests. Eed truncation and HDAC3 failed Mpz estimates remain untestable. Failed P1 mixture calibration means real fractions/responding cells remain unidentified despite normal references not reproducing Nae1 antioxidant elevation. Rat repair is a compartment warning, not neonatal replication; Figlia controls shared; GSE201623 library labels do not establish donor independence. Opposing footprints do not identify synthesis or RNA decay; IRE1 biology is known literature. No PXD043917 identification-to-LFQ substitution or age conflict resolution; human dosage/promoter and hormone branches are not solved here.

## Open questions
Bounded investigation complete as an endpoint-specific non-identifiability result, not a solved therapy. RER1 depletion is the selected independent test, after seeing existing outcomes; not a preregistered discovery. Measure total T and surface S per viable cell, S/T, calibrated newly synthesized PMP22 input, pulse-chase surface/myelin delivery yield, ER/Lamp1/insoluble pools and functional myelin in matched cultures. Verify two depletion reagents and near-endogenous RER1 addback, viability and state. Keep WT human duplication/isogenic correction distinct from L16P/+ coding-variant disease and from G150D negative comparator. No assay-specific effect size, sample-size or equivalence margin was invented.

Opposing predictions: reduced T with higher S and higher synthesis-normalized myelin yield plus improved function supports productive redistribution; higher S/T without higher S/yield, especially with Lamp1 routing, supports denominator loss/degradative escape. Higher S without function is not rescue. Changed synthesis input can explain abundance without trafficking improvement. Failed engagement/detection or survival overlap is non-identifying. For matched aggregate quantities rS=rT*rf, so opposite directions in rT and rf alone do not identify rS; mean cellular surface is mean(f*T), not the product of marginal means/medians.

